  "answer": "Project Zenith, led by Marcus Cole, was initiated in Q3 2023 to optimize cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility. The project has progressed through several phases, including design, development (led by Omar Jensen), and testing, with a prototype for secure file sharing successfully tested ahead of schedule. The team expanded by adding five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with an onboarding session scheduled for September 10th. A significant milestone was reached with the completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October, followed by a feedback collection period ending in November. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, are set to be updated effective January next year. Additionally, the compliance plan's budget has been increased to $55,000, and the team is exploring partnership opportunities with TechInnovate for AI technology integration."
